    "narrative": "Heading into today\u2019s action, **Lawrence Butler** stands out as the cornerstone of our lineup with a 74.61 efficiency score. He draws a highly favorable matchup against Wesneski, benefiting from a 10% park factor boost and a significant 13% dynamic platoon edge, positioning him as a primary engine for both power and our pursuit of stolen bases. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a high-floor anchor at 68.84 despite a poor historical BvP against Wacha; his elite batted-ball profile and top-of-the-order placement mitigate the risk. Similarly, **Cal Raleigh** offers massive upside (64.17) by exploiting a weak 4.87 xERA starter, overcoming a slight park penalty through his raw power potential.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **JJ Bleday** on the bench in favor of the higher-upside start for **Justin Crawford**. While **JJ Bleday**\u2019s 51.27 projection was respectable, he faced a sharp 14% platoon disadvantage, whereas **Justin Crawford** maintains critical utility for our stolen base targets despite facing a tough arm in Jax. We are monitoring the status of **Jonathan Aranda** and **Zack Gelof** closely; both carry \"Lineup Pending\" designations, but their projected spots in the two-hole and five-hole respectively are vital to our scoring. Should lineups shift, we have insurance in the reserves, though with **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Tyler Freeman** all unavailable due to injury or minor league assignment, our margin for error is thin. \n\nFinally, remain alert for the \"Lineup Pending\" tag on **Yainer Diaz**, **Luis Arraez**, **Bryce Harper**, and **Braden Montgomery**. While the model suggests strong outcomes, any late-scratch or shift down the order\u2014particularly for **Braden Montgomery** if he is pushed to the bottom\u2014could necessitate a pivot. We are also wary of the matchup for **Masyn Winn**, who faces the stiffest competition of the day in May; his score of 49.91 is borderline, and we are counting on his speed to provide value even if he struggles to barrel the ball against a high-tier pitcher.",
